 Jersey's four-point Democratic partisan lean anchors the presidential race", "Open seat with a term-limited incumbent president removes any incumbency edge for either party", "No state polls, expert ratings, or fundraising data exist yet, so fundamentals carry the estimate", "Both 2028 nominating contests remain unsettled, leaving candidate quality unknown"], "rationale": "New Jersey's four-point Democratic lean is the only solid evidence available: neither party has a nominee, no polls or expert ratings exist, and the term-limited incumbent leaves no incumbency effect, so the race stays at its fundamentals-based margin with wide uncertainty.", "watch": "Once both parties settle on nominees and the first New Jersey polls arrive, candidate quality or a shift in the national environment could move the state meaningfully off its lean.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "New Jersey sits about four points to the left of the country in presidential elections, and that lean is the main anchor for this open-seat contest. The incumbent Republican president is term-limited, so neither party carries an incumbency advantage, and neither major party has settled on a nominee. Coverage so far consists of national and early-state speculation about the 2028 fields, including talk of a third Chris Christie bid and shifting Democratic primary polling, none of it specific to a New Jersey general election.\n\nWith no state polls, no expert ratings, and no fundraising figures on record, the race is being judged almost entirely on the state's partisan fundamentals. That makes the expected margin modest for the Democrat and the uncertainty wide. New Jersey has usually voted Democratic in recent presidential years, but by margins that vary with the national environment, so a strong Republican nominee or a favorable national cycle could tighten the race considerably.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6761, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.642, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6472, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6427, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6518, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6522, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6491, "margin": 4.0}]}